# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 3: every per-robot line that locked on the cloud (12+ fresh seeds, 95%
# low end above 0, live turn time; coverage/shards/locks.tsv) after round 2 (PR #845) ran, locked on 12 fresh PC seeds:
#   mv (SHIELD-17 moving shield): Chameleon +9.7 (low +5.7), Artist +7.5 (+2.8), Frog +4.3 (+2.5), Tigger +3.9 (+0.4),
#      Mako +3.0 (+0.4), Hyperion +8.7 (+4.7), Shiva +6.6 (+3.7), Bezier +5.9 (+2.0, 24 seeds), Nibbler +4.5 (+1.5),
#      DarkAndDarker +4.0 (+1.8), T3 +3.7 (+0.2), R2d2 +2.7 (+0.6), Statistas +2.7 (+0.1), FloodHT +5.6 (+1.1, 24 seeds),
#      AHEB +4.8 (+0.5),
#      Princess +5.8 (+1.2), all on master 3.23
#   rp (POW-17 race power): EvBotNG +3.2 (+0.7, 24 seeds), WaveSerpent +4.6 (+1.9), Regicide +5.3 (+2.3; found by
#      round forensics: it loses low-energy wars it enters ahead)
#   pb (POW-20 power band): Atom +2.8 (+1.3), line 1.00 0.43 0.31 0.26 (BeepBoop fires about 0.5 at it); Tron +3.1
#      (+0.2, 24 seeds), line 2.08 1.00 1.00 1.00 (Saguaro fires twice our power at 20-40 energy)
#   hl (MOVE-28 stop-and-start): Flex +2.6 (+0.5, 24 seeds), Pegasus +3.6 (+2.2)
#   vj (MOVE-44 velocity jitter, off on master until this card holds it): Booring +14.0 (+12.0)
#   Older unbanked cloud locks that already failed on the PC (Yuugao, Blur, FlowerBot) or were read on the wrong
#   version (Seraphim) stay off. JointStrike hl and Splinter rp were marginal and failed 12 more cloud seeds (pooled
#   low ends -0.4 and -0.8), so they are dropped. RainbowBot mv
#   adds only +0.7 (low -0.9) on top of its shipped x5 line over 24 cloud seeds (the two fix the same loss), so it is off.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       the 24 robots   c / aa / mv / rp / pb / hl / vj (each lever arm built with only its own robots)   12 fresh seeds
#              from 43300, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks3 (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks, -locks2)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95% low end
#              is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0)
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 2 left this plan's queue state marked complete; an interrupted round 3 resumes without it.
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 2016 lock battles (24 robots, 7 arms, 12 seeds), about 57 minutes.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: every line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master.
#   - Diagnosis first:
#     mv: these shield-list robots (both halves of the list) land unshielded hits on us within 130 px (shards/shield-unshielded-C.tsv,
#     shield-unshielded-D.tsv); the opening drive keeps us off that range. Screened on 4 seeds across four boxes, the
#     leads went to 12+ fresh seeds (shards/movefield/); it pays only on the close, heavy-hit tier. mv held 3 of 3 cloud locks on the PC in round 2 (#845).
#     rp: EvBotNG wins 5/22 of the low-energy fights from behind that BeepBoop wins 24/30; WaveSerpent loses the same
#     end game (shard B attrition reads); the race power
#     pick spends less energy there (shards/attrition/).
#     pb: per energy band, a stronger robot's bullet power over ours, from paired truth logs (plans/power-band-lines.txt):
#     BeepBoop for Atom, Saguaro for Tron; the PC tests the same line the cloud lock measured.
#     hl: Flex screened +3.3 on stop-and-start and held over 24 fresh seeds (shard A); Pegasus
#     rams, and stop-and-start is the rammer escape's answer.
#     vj: Booring's pattern gun replays only history recorded at exactly our current velocity (exact double compare,
#     decompiled); BeepBoop never drives at exactly 8 or 0, so Booring falls back to linear aim, which the surf dodges.
#     The jitter moved Booring's linear share from 0.18 to 0.52 (shard A, PR #854).
#     pb (Tron): against Tron Saguaro fires 1.37 at 20-40 energy where we fire 0.66 (shards/free4/pb-tron.txt).
#   - Every robot passed the cloud lock bar first; round 1 held 8 of 13 such cloud locks on the PC (#843), round 2 held 6 of 12 (#845).
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa, which on 12 shuffled
# robots comes only near the end; aa is read in the gate (multiarm.py prints aa against c). The card halts on 30 failed
# battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24, or no battle in 30 minutes. The
# live-match step stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines on this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.23
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks3
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in mv rp pb hl vj; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks3-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 43300 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks3-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks3-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks3-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms mv rp pb hl vj --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks3-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks3-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks3-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 3 (24 robots from the field shards) locked on 12 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks3-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks3-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks3-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks3-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
